== History==
2022
*The Santa Hog Rider [[Cards|card]] was made available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Santa Hog Rider Challenge]] on 19/12/2022.
*On 26/12/2022, the Santa Hog Rider was removed from the game.
2023
*On 10/4/2023, the Santa Hog Rider was readded to the game in the Super Cards Triple Draft Event.
*On 18/4/2023, the Santa Hog Rider was removed from the game.
2024
*On 19/8/2024, the Santa Hog Rider was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 26/8/2024, the Santa Hog Rider was removed from the game.
2025
*On 27/1/2025, the Santa Hog Rider was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 3/2/2025, the Santa Hog Rider was removed from the game.

==Trivia==
*The hog that he rides is most likely a "''Phacochoerus africanus''" ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_warthog common warthog]). Common Warthogs are smaller than boars but more agile which might explain why the Santa Hog Rider can move particularly fast. Warthogs also have tusks, which is like the Santa Hog Rider's hog in Clash Royale.
*The Santa Hog Rider is tied with [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Princess]], [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], and the [[Terry]] for the longest sight range of all [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]], with a sight range of 9.5 tiles.
*The Santa Hog Rider is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Ram Rider]], and Cursed Hog.
*In the French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Turkish, Arabic, Portuguese, Persian, Indonesian, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Santa Hog Rider's name translates to "Santa Pig Rider". In the Italian, Portuguese, Thai, Finnish and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Santa Hog Rider's name translates to "Santa Wild Boar Tamer", "Santa Runner", "Santa Wild Boar Rider", and "Santa Hog Knight" respectively.
*The Santa Hog Rider bears more than a passing resemblance to [[wikipedia:Mr._T|Mr. T]] and [https://streetfighter.fandom.com/wiki/Zangief Zangief] from Street Fighter.
*His description is based on the Clash of Clans [https://youtu.be/XH3Xu1-cvII Ride of the Hog Riders commercial].
**From his description, it is implied that the [[Arenas|Arena]] has doors leading to it.
*The Santa Hog Rider is 1 of 23 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that have been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Bats]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Firecracker]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], Royal Hogs, [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], Prince, [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], Ram Rider, [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Bandit]], [[Lumberjack]], and the [[Monk]].
*When the Santa Hog Rider is deployed, he will occasionally yell "''Hog Riderrrrr!''"
**The Santa Hog Rider is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Wizard]], Hog Rider, [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Dark Prince, [[Bowler]], Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], Princess, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], Lumberjack, Mother Witch, [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the Terry.
*Unlike the [[Royal Ghost]], troops affected by the Invisibility [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] do not reveal themselves when attacking, meaning the only way to damage them is via spells or through indirect means (e.g the [[Electro Spirit|Electro Spirit's]] chain attack).
*The Santa Hog Rider is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].

